<title>USA: Disney to sell Institutional Investor - NYT.</title>
<headline>Disney to sell Institutional Investor - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Walt Disney Co is expected soon to sign a pact to sell Institutional Investor publications to Euromoney Publications Plc for $120-$130 million, The New York Times said.</p>
<p>In its Monday edition the paper cited &quot;executives familiar with the negotiations&quot; as saying other potential suitors including the Thompson Financial Publishing Group and Pearson Plc have shown strong interest in buying Institutional Investor, but those companies had recently dropped out.</p>
<p>Institutional Investor and Euromoney have competed for years for the reading time and desk space of financiers and investors, the story said.</p>
<p>Euromoney is 63 percent owned by Daily Mail and General Trust Plc, publishers of the Daily Mail of Britain.</p>
